sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Client
    participant B as Booking service
    participant S as Supplier adapter
    participant P as Payment service
    U->>B: POST /v1/flight-bookings with offer_id and Idempotency-Key
    B->>S: re-price offer
    S-->>B: current price and availability
    alt price changed
        B-->>U: 409 price changed, new price, confirm to continue
    end
    B->>S: create PNR with reference = booking_id
    S-->>B: PNR locator, hold until T plus 30 min
    B->>P: authorize amount, idempotency key = booking_id
    P-->>B: authorized
    B->>S: issue ticket for PNR
    alt ticketing succeeds
        S-->>B: ticket numbers
        B->>P: capture
        B-->>U: 200 TICKETED
    else ticketing fails or times out
        B->>P: void authorization
        B->>S: release PNR if held
        B-->>U: 409 could not ticket, offering next supplier for same flight
    end
    Note over B,S: Any supplier timeout moves the booking to PENDING_RESOLUTION. The resolver looks the PNR up by booking_id before anything is retried.
